module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.shape_predicate_reads_only_the_head_so_a_container_passes_as_its_element

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data shape_predicate_reads_only_the_head_so_a_container_passes_as_its_element: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "shape_predicate_reads_only_the_head_so_a_container_passes_as_its_element" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**A STRUCTURAL PREDICATE THAT INSPECTS ONLY THE FIRST CHILD CANNOT DISTINGUISH A CONTAINER OF N ELEMENTS FROM ONE ELEMENT, so the container is admitted AS an element and elements 2..N are silently dropped by whatever consumes the match.** The invalid state is a total, pure, fail-closed-looking walk that returns a population of the right TYPE and the wrong CARDINALITY, with no refusal anywhere: the consumer reads the accepted value's head, produces a well-formed partial answer, and reports Accepted. The harm is DESIGN section 5's forbidden case rather than a rung: a fabricated plausible output, here a syntactically valid target module missing most of its declarations, which compiles and therefore fails no downstream check either.",

    "**SPECIMEN WITH A RECEIPT, measured 2026-09-09 on the v2 production Rust door.** `v2.compiler.emit_produced` `produced_decl_node_is_decl` asked whether a node was a `Conj` whose FIRST child is a `Named` edge into an `Arrow`, and `produced_decl_conjs_in_tree` recorded such a node and stopped descending. But a resolved .dag module carries one `Named`-into-`Arrow` edge PER DECLARATION on a single shell `Conj`, so the SHELL satisfied that predicate; the walk recorded the shell as one declaration, and `emit_produced_decl` -- which reads `children[0]` -- emitted declaration 1 and dropped 2..N. Measured through `observe_provenanced_rust_emission_from_ingest` over an ingested two-declaration module: `ArtifactProduced`, carrying exactly the first declaration. Enrolled evidence: `v2.test.claim.self_host.rust_module_emission_population`, whose count arm read 1 before the repair and 2 after, one stage BEFORE emission so a correct concatenation could not stand in for a correct collection.",

    "**WHY IT SURVIVED, and this is the transferable part.** Every existing witness over the same fold was green throughout, because each one HANDED THE FOLD A LIST OF DECLARATIONS IT HAD BUILT ITSELF (`ingested_add_decl_node`, `table_fixture_add_decl_node`) and therefore never exercised the collector at all. A fixture that constructs the population cannot discriminate a defect in DERIVING the population, however thoroughly it pins the fold's ordering, separators and refusal propagation -- and the ordering witness in particular reads as if it covers exactly this. The specimen must be the real ingested tree.",

    "**THE COINCIDENCE THAT HID IT AND THE DEAD REFUSAL THAT LOOKED LIKE A WALL.** At N=1 the shell and the declaration ARE the same node, so the only shape the door was exercised on was correct by accident, and every byte-level golden agreed. Above it the composition carried an explicit surplus arm refusing `rust_module_emission_decl_ambiguous` -- which was UNREACHABLE from any real module, because the collector never produced a surplus to refuse. **A REFUSAL FOR THE CASE A DEFECTIVE PRODUCER CANNOT PRODUCE READS AS A WALL AND IS A DECORATION** (DESIGN section 4b: ask whether the check's RED is authorable before writing the check). The lane's premise was that this arm was the admission ceiling to relax; it was never load-bearing, and relaxing it alone would have published partial modules under a wider admission.",

    "**RECOGNITION RULE: when a predicate decides a node's ROLE, name the two roles it must separate and check whether both can present the same first child.** A container and its first element routinely can. The repair direction is to move the predicate onto the EDGE that actually carries the role -- here a declaration IS the named edge into an arrow, and no per-declaration node exists in the tree at all -- rather than to add a count or a depth guard to the node predicate, which re-states the same conflation with a bound on it. The field tell needs no execution: a SECOND private collector answering the same question nearby. `v2.workflow.realization_attempt` `collect_arrows` walked the shell's edges one-per-declaration and was correct; its existence beside this authority is the static symptom, and DESIGN section 3 already prices the fork.",

    "**RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder -- silent wrongness, which section 4b states is not a rung. CURRENT RUNG AFTER REPAIR: 2 (mechanically preventable): the walk is correct and an executing discriminating RED holds it, but the invalid predicate remains writable and the guarantee depends on that witness staying enrolled. CEILING: 4 (structurally impossible), because whether a node's role predicate can be satisfied by a container of that role is decidable from declarations the Node tree already carries. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a CAPABILITY and not an artifact: a structural role predicate declares the role it decides and the carrier that role inhabits, so a predicate whose match is satisfiable by a container of its own role fails to compile. That capability does not exist today (measured 2026-09-09: role predicates in the corpus are ordinary Bool functions over Node with no declared subject role), so this is a stall whose trigger is an absent language capability, not a scheduled edit.**",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
